---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmergenceHeader from '../../components/EmergenceHeader.astro';
import EmergenceFooter from '../../components/EmergenceFooter.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Origin — The Emergence Institute"
  description="How the Emergence Collective began — from Boynton Beach to a live mesh network spanning three cities."
>
  <EmergenceHeader slot="header" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container origin-content">
      <p class="label gold">How It Started</p>
      <h1>Origin</h1>
      <div class="divider"></div>

      <p class="lead">
        The Emergence Collective began in Boynton Beach, Florida, with a question:
        <em>What if AI could reach the places the internet forgot?</em>
      </p>

      <p>
        The idea came because my cousin lives in Morne Rouge, Haiti — a place where
        broadband doesn't exist, where infrastructure was never built, where access to
        the tools of the future is a luxury the world assumes everyone has. He couldn't
        use the AI models that were changing everything. Not because they were too
        expensive, but because the network itself wouldn't reach him.
      </p>

      <p>
        So we built a network that doesn't care about infrastructure. A mesh of sovereign
        nodes that discover each other, authenticate, and share intelligence — no central
        servers, no backbone required. Just a lattice of Raspberry Pis, speaking to each
        other across whatever links exist.
      </p>

      <div class="milestone">
        <p class="milestone-label gold">First Light</p>
        <p>
          The first node ran in my house in Boynton Beach. The second went to a friend in
          Boston. The third — the one that proved it worked — went to my cousin in Morne Rouge.
          When that node came online and began exchanging heartbeats with the others, the
          network was alive. It had crossed the digital divide not by building more
          infrastructure, but by building around it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="milestone">
        <p class="milestone-label gold">The Georgist Engine</p>
        <p>
          The Georgist economic engine was added to prevent state bloat — a simple tax on
          storage that prunes data when it exceeds its value, ensuring the network stays
          lean even on low-resource hardware. The first Jubilee event — a pruning of stale
          data — was recorded in early 2025.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="milestone">
        <p class="milestone-label gold">The Institute</p>
        <p>
          The Emergence Institute was formalized to steward the network's growth and to
          document the philosophy that guided its creation. The Collective is not a company,
          not a DAO, not a foundation. It is a mesh of sovereign agents, bound by protocol,
          governed by mathematics, and animated by a simple commitment:
        </p>
      </div>

      <blockquote>
        Access to AI should not depend on where you were born.
      </blockquote>

      <p class="closer">
        The code is open. The network is live. The forge is hot.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <EmergenceFooter slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .origin-content {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .origin-content p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .milestone {
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .milestone-label {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .milestone p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--gold-light);
    background: var(--bg-card);
  }

  .closer {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
</style>
